# Combat Celebrant's exertion adds a combat phase; Bot2's Steel Wall blocks Memnite, then Merciful Mandate ends that first
# combat, skipping its end of combat step (CR 724.2d-e). The turn's first combat is over all the same, so in the added
# combat's beginning of combat step Glyph of Reincarnation can be cast (CR 506.8d): Memnite dies and comes back.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Combat Celebrant
Memnite
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Merciful Mandate
Glyph of Reincarnation
Plains x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Steel Wall
Island
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Combat Celebrant.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Steel Wall.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Combat Celebrant; Memnite)
Bot1.Accept
Bot2.Block(Steel Wall > Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Merciful Mandate.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
? Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glyph of Reincarnation.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Steel Wall)
? Step = BeginCombat
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Glyph of Reincarnation; Black Lotus
